<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scaliger Tombs</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Arche Scaligere</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scaliger">Scaliger</a> Tombs, or Arche Scaligere, are a group of Gothic funerary monuments in Verona, beside the church of Santa Maria Antica, built for the della Scala lords of the city in the 14th century. The tombs of Cangrande I, Mastino II and Cansignorio, crowned with equestrian statues, are among the finest examples of Gothic sculpture in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scaliger-tombs.jpg" alt="Scaliger Tombs" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arche_scaligere_(Verona).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
